== VRF collision handling (vector TB, scratch counters, not committed) ==
same-row read+write cycles: 136,168 (port A 20,584, B 20,671, C 94,913),
  all with a full-word write -> served by the bypass, replica not read
retry (stall) cycles: 12
element writes: 378,358, of which full-word 375,165, partial 3,193
vector TB cycles: 13,232,168 (round-2 RTL: 13,232,156)
With write combining disabled (retry only): 13,373,624 cycles (+1.07%);
  trial-weighted op cycles +9.8%, single-cycle integer ops up to +49%.

== Collision-mode models (permanent in srammacro) ==
sky130 OpenRAM and fakeram45 1R1W models return whole-word garbage for a
same-address read and write.
  round-2 RTL (fd55986) on these models:  VEC TB FAIL (566 fakeram45, 565 sky130)
  round-3 RTL:                            VEC TB PASS on both; srammacro PASS
Mutations of round-3 RTL (vector TB, sky130 models):
  colliding reads sent to the macro (no bypass)     FAIL (568 failures)
  no write combining (retry only)                   PASS, 13,373,624 cycles
  no retry                                          partial-collision assertion fires
  old-word staleness tracking off                   FAIL (7 failures)
Earlier mutations (wrapper RTL unchanged since): VRF capture register
removed -> FAIL on both families; sky130 L1 half select stuck -> cache
tests FAIL; L1 capture register removed -> still PASS (kept by design).

